---
// The loop from the business card, one step per term.
const steps = [
  {
    term: "Measure",
    detail:
      "Four DORA metrics cover speed and stability, and product owner task cycle time shows whether the work moves the business. Measuring and regularly tracking these five will help us determine success.",
  },
  {
    term: "Diagnose",
    detail:
    "Now that we can see our problem in the numbers, it's time to find the bottleneck keeping us there.",
  },
  {
    term: "Fix",
    detail:
      "Next, we'll work together to implement the solution.",
  },
  {
    term: "Repeat",
    detail:
    "Problem solving is a process of iteration. We'll remeasure to see how well our solution worked and course-correct if we need to.",
  },
];
---

<section id="services" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t border-rule py-20 lg:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <h2
        class="font-display text-[clamp(1.9rem,3.6vw,2.75rem)] font-medium leading-[1.12] tracking-[-0.015em]"
      >
        How it works
      </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        We start with the gold standard for determining development team productivity. 
        How fast is my team going?
        How much time does my software spend out of order?
        Is the work my dev team is doing moving the business forward?
      </p>
    </div>

    <dl class="mt-14 grid gap-x-12 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        steps.map((s, i) => (
          <div class="border-t border-green py-5">
            <dt class="flex items-baseline gap-3 font-display text-xl font-medium text-green">
              <span class="label">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
              {s.term}
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 max-w-md leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{s.detail}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
